An election.

The votes for a candidate (text) in some ballots (a list of texts) is a whole number:
the number of ballots in the ballots where the ballot is the candidate.

A candidate (text) wins in some ballots (a list of texts) when:
the votes for the candidate in the ballots times 2 is more than the length of the ballots.

Suppose ballots is a list of "ana", "bo", "ana" and "ana".
For example, the votes for "ana" in ballots is 3.
For example, the votes for "cy" in ballots is 0.
For example, "ana" wins in ballots.
For example, "bo" wins in ballots is false.
